    <briefdescription>
<para>Exponential back-off retry policy for transient wire-protocol faults. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Delay formula (all values in milliseconds): <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">delay(n)<sp/>=<sp/>min(<sp/><ref refid="structthemis_1_1network_1_1_retry_policy_1af8166bb573b47da9c1419ec2d28f8293" kindref="member">base_delay_ms</ref><sp/>*<sp/>2^n<sp/>+<sp/>uniform(0,<sp/><ref refid="structthemis_1_1network_1_1_retry_policy_1a32c481f15d4a90075ec68a54a5d6bb86" kindref="member">jitter_ms</ref>),<sp/><ref refid="structthemis_1_1network_1_1_retry_policy_1a4a728b309e4e9808b35e15166efa3b19" kindref="member">max_delay_ms</ref><sp/>)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Retryable error codes (POSIX):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>ECONNRESET — connection reset by peer</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>ETIMEDOUT — operation timed out</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>EAGAIN / EWOULDBLOCK — transient resource unavailability</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The policy object is value-copyable and thread-safe for read access; <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1network_1_1_retry_policy_1a831cd7b89db8f0cff3e733efdd23eaa4" kindref="member">computeDelay()</ref></computeroutput> uses a thread-local PRNG so no external synchronisation is required. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
